---
import { security as s, links } from "../data/facts";
const layers = [
  { t: "Architecture", d: "Plan before reading. Permissions in SQL. Read-only role. Approval as a graph interrupt. These hold even if the model is fully fooled." },
  { t: "Output sanitizing", d: "Images removed and links reduced to text, so a hijacked answer can't send your data to someone else's server. The UI also blocks remote images." },
  { t: "Input hygiene", d: "Paragraphs that address an AI are redacted from passages, and delimiter tags are escaped so a document can't close its own quote." },
  { t: "Prompting", d: "Evidence is marked as data and followed by a reminder. Useful, but never the only layer." },
];
---
<section class="section security" id="security">
  <div class="wrap sec-grid">
    <div class="sec-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow reveal">Security</span>
      <h2 class="h2 reveal" style="--d:1">Assume the model <span class="serif glow-text">will</span> be fooled.</h2>
      <p class="lede reveal" style="--d:2">
        In the first attack run, a vendor notice planted in the knowledge base told the model to end
        every answer with a secret code. It obeyed twice. The phishing link it was also told to add
        had already been stripped by code. That's the whole philosophy: prompts are suggestions,
        code is a guarantee.
      </p>

      <dl class="sec-stats reveal" style="--d:3">
        <div><dt><span data-count={s.defended}>{s.defended}</span>/{s.attacks}</dt><dd>injection attacks defended<br /><span class="muted">first run: {s.defendedFirst}/{s.attacks}</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt><span data-count={s.blocked}>{s.blocked}</span>/{s.scenarios}</dt><dd>live attempts to bypass approval, blocked</dd></div>
        <div><dt>0</dt><dd>unauthorized executions across these and {s.unitScenarios} unit scenarios</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <a class="sec-link reveal" href={links.security} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the security report →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="rings reveal" style="--d:2" aria-label="Four layers of defense, from the outermost to the innermost">
      {layers.map((l, i) => (
        <div class={`ring r${i}`} tabindex="0">
          <span class="ring-t">{l.t}</span>
          <span class="ring-d">{l.d}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
      <div class="core"><span class="mono">model</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sec-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 72px; align-items: center; }
  .sec-stats { display: grid; gap: 0; margin: 40px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sec-stats div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: 16px; align-items: baseline; padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sec-stats dt { font-size: 38px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .sec-stats dd { margin: 0; color: var(--text-2); font-size: 15.5px; }
  .sec-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 24px; color: var(--sun); font-size: 15px; }

  .rings { position: relative; width: 100%; max-width: 520px; aspect-ratio: 1; margin: 0 auto; }
  .ring {
    position: absolute;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 3.2%;
    text-align: center;
    transition: border-color 0.4s, background 0.4s;
    outline: none;
  }
  .r0 { inset: 0; background: radial-gradient(circle, transparent 60%, rgba(255, 138, 61, 0.05)); }
  .r1 { inset: 12%; }
  .r2 { inset: 24%; }
  .r3 { inset: 36%; }
  .ring-t { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-2); }
  .ring-d {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: min(240px, 46vw);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0.96);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-2);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(14, 16, 22, 0.94);
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.3s, transform 0.4s var(--ease);
    z-index: 3;
  }
  .ring:hover, .ring:focus-visible { border-color: rgba(255, 181, 71, 0.6); background-color: rgba(255, 181, 71, 0.04); }
  .ring:hover > .ring-d, .ring:focus-visible > .ring-d { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1); }
  .ring:hover .ring-t { color: var(--sun); }
  .core {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 46%;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #2a1d14, #0b0b0d 70%);
    box-shadow: 0 0 60px rgba(255, 138, 61, 0.45), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 181, 71, 0.4);
    color: var(--sun);
    font-size: 11px;
    animation: breathe 4s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes breathe { 50% { box-shadow: 0 0 90px rgba(255, 138, 61, 0.65), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 181, 71, 0.6); } }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .sec-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 56px; }
    .sec-stats div { grid-template-columns: 96px 1fr; }
  }
</style>
